            <ArticleTitle>Traumatic dissection of the left circumflex artery after a fall from height.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>772-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0003319707306449</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present the case of a healthy 40-year-old man who developed a myocardial infarction because of traumatic dissection of the left circumflex coronary artery following a fall from height. To our knowledge, this is the first time that a traumatic lesion of the left circumflex artery is being reported after a fall.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
